{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Number","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" = [","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending\/number-swift.typealias"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The ending-number type is used to specify the positive integers (without leading zeros) of the ending element.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"An empty array is used when software knows that an ending is present, but cannot determine the type of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ending.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"typealias","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Number"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Number"}],"roleHeading":"Type Alias","extendedModule":"IvorMXL","title":"MXLEnding.Number","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLEndingV6Numbera"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/Number-swift.typealias"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding"]]},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLEnding":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The ending type represents multiple (e.g. first and second) endings. Typically, the start type is associated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the left barline of the first measure in an ending. The stop and discontinue types are associated with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the right barline of the last measure in an ending. Stop is used when the ending mark concludes with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"downward jog, as is typical for first endings. Discontinue is used when there is no downward jog, as is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"typical for second endings that do not conclude a piece. The length of the jog can be specified using the end-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"length attribute. The text-x and text-y attributes are offsets that specify where the baseline of the start of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the ending text appears, relative to the start of the ending line."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding","title":"MXLEnding","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLEnding"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLEnding"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLEnding/Number-swift.typealias":{"title":"MXLEnding.Number","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending\/number-swift.typealias","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/Number-swift.typealias","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Number","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Number","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The ending-number type is used to specify the positive integers (without leading zeros) of the ending element."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"An empty array is used when software knows that an ending is present, but cannot determine the type of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ending."}]}}}